    "problem_statement": "Class dictionary extraction fails for multiple inheritance\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen extracting class dictionaries for classes with multiple inheritance, the `_extract_class_dict` function incorrectly removes attributes that should be preserved. This affects pickling of classes that inherit from multiple base classes.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport cloudpickle\nfrom cloudpickle.cloudpickle import _extract_class_dict\n\nclass A(int):\n    \"\"\"A docstring\"\"\"\n    \n    def method(self):\n        return 'a'\n\nclass B:\n    \"\"\"B docstring\"\"\"\n    B_CONSTANT = 42\n    \n    def method(self):\n        return 'b'\n\nclass C(A, B):\n    C_CONSTANT = 43\n    \n    def method_c(self):\n        return 'c'\n\n# This should preserve C's own attributes\nclsdict = _extract_class_dict(C)\nprint(\"Extracted keys:\", list(clsdict.keys()))\nprint(\"Expected keys: ['C_CONSTANT', '__doc__', 'method_c']\")\n```\n\nThe extracted dictionary is missing expected keys that are specific to class C and should not be filtered out during the inheritance filtering process."
